index a74e8ee..c78b02b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,29 +1,76 @@
 # Borealis Guides
 
-A simple Sphinx documentation starter with a persistent sidebar, built-in full-text search, breadcrumbs, mobile navigation, and editable Markdown pages. The teal, blue, purple, magenta, and navy theme follows the supplied colour reference.
+Bilingual Zensical documentation prototype with User Guide, Admin Guide, and
+API Guide tabs, a section sidebar on the left, and a page table of contents on
+the right. The homepage uses a translucent blue-purple panel and responsive
+guide cards. Light and dark modes have distinct code surfaces.
 
-This is a design prototype, not an approved replacement for the current Borealis guides. The content pages are explicitly marked as editorial outlines. No existing guide text has been migrated.
+Content pages remain editorial outlines, not approved operational guidance.
+French landing pages are draft translations. Pages without a French source
+show their English content with a French notice.
 
-## Preview locally
+## Install and preview
 
 ```sh
 python -m venv .venv
 # macOS/Linux:
 source .venv/bin/activate
-# Windows PowerShell: .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
+# Windows Git Bash instead: source .venv/Scripts/activate
+# Windows PowerShell instead: .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
 python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
-python -m sphinx -W --keep-going -b html docs _build/html
-python -m http.server 8000 --directory _build/html
+zensical serve
 ```
 
-Open http://localhost:8000.
+Open the local URL printed by Zensical. Plain `zensical serve` is useful for
+English layout editing on Windows, but it does not build the bilingual site.
+The pinned `zensical-i18n` wrapper has triggered a Windows backslash-path panic
+in our local setup. Use Linux, WSL, or the Ubuntu GitHub Actions build for the
+complete bilingual build:
 
-## Edit the guide
+```sh
+zensical-i18n build --clean --strict
+python scripts/check_site.py
+python -m http.server 8000 --directory site
+```
+
+Open http://localhost:8000/ and test the language selector. For live editing of
+one language on Linux/WSL, use `zensical-i18n serve --lang fr`. This preview
+serves only one language; use the full build above to test switching languages.
+
+## Edit pages and translations
 
-Edit `docs/*.md`. Add new pages to a `toctree` in `docs/index.md`. Change colours and spacing in `docs/_static/borealis.css`. Site title, theme, and GitHub edit links live in `docs/conf.py`.
+Edit English Markdown files in `docs/`. Add French translations alongside them:
+`find-data.md` and `find-data.fr.md`. Keep links unsuffixed in both languages,
+for example `[Trouver des données](../find-data.md)`. The build resolves them
+within the current language. English is published at the root and French at
+`fr/`, with matching page-to-page language links.
+
+Navigation and translated labels live in `zensical.toml`. Keep
+`navigation.tabs`, `navigation.indexes`, and `toc.follow`; do not enable
+`toc.integrate` if you want the right-hand contents column. Add `##` headings
+to populate that column. Sidebars collapse automatically on smaller screens.
+The header logo links to the homepage, so the top navigation has just three
+guide tabs. Existing root-level Markdown paths are retained.
+
+Custom styles live in `docs/stylesheets/extra.css`. Edit the existing rules
+instead of appending overlapping theme patches. The logo is a local copy of
+[Borealis's homepage logo](https://borealisdata.ca/assets/img/homepage-logo.png),
+stored at `docs/images/borealis-logo.png`. Its header height is 48px and its
+homepage width is 240px. To substitute an approved SVG, put it in `docs/images/`
+and update the `logo`/`favicon` settings and both homepage Markdown references.
+The logo remains the property of its owner; no brand licence is implied.
 
 ## GitHub Pages
 
-The included workflow validates every push and pull request. To publish, select **Settings → Pages → Source → GitHub Actions**, then run the **Documentation** workflow on `main`. Deployment uses GitHub's `github-pages` environment. The site URL will be https://thisisbillie.github.io/borealis-guide/.
+The Documentation workflow builds both languages on Ubuntu and checks the
+generated links and assets on pushes to `main` and pull requests. Dependencies
+are pinned to Zensical 0.0.74 and zensical-i18n 0.3.0. The uploaded Pages artifact
+is `site/`.
+
+Publication remains manual: select **Settings → Pages → Source → GitHub Actions**,
+then run **Actions → Documentation → Run workflow** on `main`. The existing
+deployment condition is retained; a push or pull request only builds and checks.
+The site URL is https://thisisbillie.github.io/borealis-guide/.
 
-Review and replace the editorial outlines before using this as official documentation. No content or brand licence is implied by this starter.
+The repository previously used Sphinx. Its configuration and templates are
+retained in Git history. The current workflow uses `zensical.toml` only.
